@prefix pair: <http://w3id.org/airiskkg/pair-ai#> .
@prefix beam: <http://w3id.org/beam/core#> .
@prefix bpmn: <https://sBPMN.github.io/2.0/classes#> .
@prefix bp:   <https://sBPMN.github.io/2.0/properties#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dct:  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix vann: <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .

<http://w3id.org/airiskkg/context>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dct:title "PAIR-AI Business Context Bridge"@en ;
    dct:description """Joins a business process model to the AI architectures it
uses. Three layers, joined by refinement and never by subsumption: the business
layer says what the organisation does, the architecture layer says how one AI
capability is built, and the pattern layer matches motifs over the second.

A BPMN activity is NOT a beam:Process and must never be aligned to one. Every
match query types its step node as `?step a/rdfs:subClassOf* beam:Process`, so
subsuming activities under it would make every business activity a candidate
motif node - and the input contract, which requires each beam:Process to use or
produce a resource, would reject every process model outright."""@en ;
    dct:source <https://sbpmn.github.io/2.0/> ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "pair" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "http://w3id.org/airiskkg/pair-ai#" ;
    owl:imports <http://w3id.org/beam/core#> .

### The bridge

pair:refinedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "refined by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """The AI system that carries out this business activity: one box
in the process diagram, expanded into an architecture graph.

PAIR owns this rather than reusing sbpmn:calledElement, whose range is
unconstrained and which would therefore accept it. Reusing it would hard-code the
sBPMN namespace into every submitted architecture and foreclose swapping the
process ontology later; the bridge belongs to whichever project spans both layers,
and that is this one.

Attach it to the activity that invokes the capability. A bpmn:serviceTask is the
ordinary case - one activity, one system. A bpmn:callActivity or bpmn:subProcess
is the agentic case, where the capability is itself a process."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain bpmn:activity ;
    rdfs:range beam:System ;
    rdfs:seeAlso bp:calledElement .

pair:businessFollows a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:label "business follows"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Derived, never annotated: one flow node is reachable from
another along BPMN sequence flow.

It exists because bp:sourceRef and bp:targetRef are declared on five classes -
sequenceFlow, messageFlow, dataAssociation, association and conversationLink. A
property path written straight over them walks out of control flow, through a
data association, and back in somewhere unrelated, and the result looks like
evidence. Materializing one typed hop means every condition downstream can use a
plain transitive path and cannot make that mistake.

Transitive so a gateway, a wait, or an intervening activity between the AI step
and a later control does not hide it."""@en ;
    rdfs:domain bpmn:flowNode ;
    rdfs:range bpmn:flowNode .

pair:BusinessFlowDerivation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Business Flow Derivation"@en ;
    skos:definition """Marker output type for implementations that derive
relations over the business process layer rather than over the architecture.

A distinct type from pair:DataCategoryPropagation because these carry no data
category and assert nothing about content - the same reason mitigation rewrites
have their own type. Both run in the pipeline's derivation phase, before any
motif is matched."""@en .

### Registration

<http://w3id.org/airiskkg/patterns#BusinessFlow_DerivationOQP>
    a pair:PatternImplementation ;
    rdfs:label "Typed reachability over BPMN sequence flow"@en ;
    pair:implementationPath "ontology/context/implementation/business_flow.rq" ;
    pair:producesOutputType pair:BusinessFlowDerivation .
